@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@firebaseIdToken = paste-a-firebase-id-token-here

### 1. Create a test Firebase user in the local emulator (NOT production).
POST http://127.0.0.1:9099/identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signUp?key=demo-key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "diego@example.com",
  "password": "MiClaveSegura2026!",
  "returnSecureToken": true
}

### 2. Firebase email/password sign-in (emulator); copy idToken above.
POST http://127.0.0.1:9099/identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signInWithPassword?key=demo-key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "diego@example.com",
  "password": "MiClaveSegura2026!",
  "returnSecureToken": true
}

### 3. Register local IAM account, ranch and Owner membership.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ranch-units
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fundo San José",
  "region": "Apurímac",
  "district": "Andahuaylas",
  "estimatedHeadCount": 120,
  "latitude": -13.6556,
  "longitude": -73.3878
}

### 4. Validate the Firebase identity and retrieve local account/memberships.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idToken": "{{firebaseIdToken}}"
}

### 5. Current identity.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

### 6. Ranch access (verify email in Firebase first, then sign in again).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ranch-units/REPLACE_WITH_RANCH_UUID
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
